 `.env` uses the usual dotenv syntax: `KEY=value`, optional single or double quotes around the value, an optional leading `export `, and `#` comment lines.
 
+`python -m payhook doctor` prints every setting with its effective value and source (`env`, `.env` or `default`). Secrets (`PAYHOOK_API_TOKEN`, `PAYHOOK_WEBHOOK_SECRET`) are never printed, only whether they are set and their length, so the output is safe to paste into a support ticket.
